# Calliope honesty slice — 2026-08-13
#
# GOAL, this slice only: a traveller who already said enough is not re-asked,
# not sent to the wrong city, not silently locked to an airline, and not told
# we are searching a leg we are not searching.
#
# NOT "finish Calliope" and NOT "close #2168". Do not close #2168.
#
# G2 < 5s and G3 > 80% are OUT of pass/fail. C5 reports each of G1-G4 as
# met / missed / n too small. A metric that cannot yet be measured is not a
# gate, and saying so is the point of the slice.
#
# IN:  #2257 #2173 #2274 #2230 #2216 #2254
# OUT: #2174 #2176 #2175 #2217 #2220 #2235 #2242 #2243
#
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THREE AMENDMENTS to the plan as written. Reasons, not preferences.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A1. #2173 MOVES OUT OF WAVE 1. The plan contradicted itself.
#     It says "#2257 first so later replay numbers mean something" and then
#     schedules #2173 in wave 1, parallel with #2257 - which does not merge
#     until after its wave-2 critic. So the C5 baseline would be measured
#     with the instrument #2257 is fixing, and the 08-14 re-run would
#     disagree with it for reasons unrelated to the Conductor.
#     -> #2173 runs AFTER #2257 lands. If that is unacceptable for timing,
#        the report MUST state which numbers were taken pre-fix. It may not
#        silently mix them.
#
# A2. EVERY PROD PROBE GETS A CONTROL, not just Malmo.
#     The plan gets the diacritics probe right (unaccented first, then
#     accented) and then asks for "fly Malta in June (no carrier lock)" with
#     no control. A probe that finds no lock is INDISTINGUISHABLE from a probe
#     that cannot see locks. Same for the hotels-only prose check.
#     -> Controls are mandatory. See PROD PROBES below.
#     This is the exact defect the slice exists to fix, applied to its own
#     verification. On 2026-08-12 a 904KB prod-bundle probe returned 0 for the
#     target AND 0 for the control, and every 0 was meaningless.
#
# A3. BUDGET THE CORRECTION ROUNDS. The plan has verdicts and no loop-back.
#     Every PR on 08-12 and 08-13 took one or two rounds after its critic, and
#     those rounds were where the value was. Six waves with no allowance will
#     slip on the first SHIP IT WITH X, and the temptation is to wave it
#     through. Assume ONE correction round per code branch. Four code branches
#     -> four rounds. If a branch needs a third, that is a signal about the
#     branch, not about the schedule.
#
# DROPPED from the plan: "if dispatch is unproven since 07-30, one throwaway
# seat first". Dispatch is proven - 15+ producer and critic seats ran on
# 08-12/13 with no dispatch failures. Skip the throwaway.
#
# KEPT, and worth naming because it is better than what ran on 08-12:
#   FAIL-FIRST TESTS ARE THEIR OWN WAVE, BEFORE IMPLEMENTATION.
#   Waves 1 and 4 write tests; waves 2 and 5 write code. A test written by
#   someone who already knows the implementation tends to test the
#   implementation. Separating the seats is the stronger discipline. Adopt
#   this generally, not just here.
#
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ORDER
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
1 | test-engineer | #2257 fix the replay sink so grant_route survives. Everything measured later depends on this being right first. | task/2257-replay-grant-route
1 | test-engineer | #2274 FAIL-FIRST TESTS ONLY. Accented city names normalise to empty because ResolveIATA does an exact uppercase lookup against unaccented keys. Do not implement. | task/2274-iata-fold
1 | test-engineer | #2230 FAIL-FIRST TESTS ONLY. A fuzzy carrier match in "fly-X" frames mints a hard carrier lock from ordinary words. Keep "fly luftansa" working. Do not implement. | task/2230-carrier-frames
#
2 | backend-critic | Review #2257. | task/2257-replay-grant-route
2 | go-backend | Implement #2274. Unicode fold; no accented keys in the table. | task/2274-iata-fold
2 | go-backend | Implement #2230. Kill the false locks, keep the real one. | task/2230-carrier-frames
#
3 | backend-critic | Review #2274. | task/2274-iata-fold
3 | backend-critic | Review #2230. | task/2230-carrier-frames
3 | test-engineer | #2216 + #2254 FAIL-FIRST TESTS ONLY, one branch. Moved up from wave 4 so wave 3 is not critics-only. | task/2216-2254-ready-prose
#
4 | go-backend | Implement #2216 + #2254 on that tree. | task/2216-2254-ready-prose
4 | devops | #2173 C5 baseline report + re-runnable query. AFTER #2257 lands (A1). State G1-G4 as met/missed/n-too-small. | task/2173-c5-baseline
#
5 | backend-critic | Review the combined #2216 + #2254 tree. | task/2216-2254-ready-prose
#
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LANDING — mine, not a seat
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   #2257, #2274, #2230 land separately. Disjoint files.
#   #2216 + #2254 land as ONE PR. Same Conductor/recap package: two CLEAN PRs
#   can still redden main.
#   HARD GATE: before landing any two that can couple, merge them LOCALLY and
#   run the suite. CLEAN is not safety. Proven twice now - #2568/#2561 shared
#   no file and would have reddened main; #2594/#2596 shared two and did
#   conflict while both reported clean.
#   #2173 is a report. I read it. No code critic.
#
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PROD PROBES — control FIRST, every time (A2)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   diacritics   control: "Malmo"  -> expect a resolved city
#                target:  "Malmö"  -> expect the SAME resolution
#
#   carrier      control: "fly Lufthansa to Malta in June"
#                         -> expect a carrier lock, PROVING locks are visible
#                target:  "fly to Malta in June"
#                         -> expect NO lock
#                Without the control, "no lock" and "cannot see locks" are the
#                same observation.
#
#   prose        control: a trip request -> expect "flights" in the narration
#                target:  "just a hotel in Lisbon" -> expect NO "flights"
#
#   Say what could NOT be verified. That beats a green probe implying coverage
#   it does not have.
#
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DONE WHEN
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   1. A critic verdict on every code branch.
#   2. Four fail-firsts watched RED then GREEN. Watched, not asserted.
#   3. Combined #2216 + #2254 suite green, run from apps/api.
#   4. Replay: hotel-only confirmation case clean, grant_route countable.
#   5. C5 file exists under docs/qa/, dated, G1-G4 stated honestly.
#   6. All six prod probes run, each with its control first.
#   7. What could not be verified is written down.
#   8. #2168 STAYS OPEN.
#
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CARRIED FORWARD — in every brief until they live in a skill file
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   Module root is apps/api. `go test` from the repo root gives
#   [setup failed], which reads exactly like a real break.
#
#   FIVE ways a proof has lied on this repo in the last week:
#   a) a perl -0pi syntax error left the source pristine and the suite passed
#   b) a mutation landed in the error branch and failed to COMPILE; a naive
#      runner reports that as RED
#   c) git clean -fd deleted worktree node_modules symlinks, so six "reds"
#      were module-resolution errors
#   d) a nil-deref panic killed the test binary early: two failures at 2.7s
#      against a 14.3s baseline, reading as the OPPOSITE conclusion.
#      RECORD THE BASELINE DURATION. Better, compare COLLECTED TEST COUNTS.
#   e) NEW, 2026-08-13: a DIRTY PR gets no merge ref, so GitHub runs NOTHING,
#      and `check-runs` returns an EMPTY array. Zero pending, zero failing,
#      reads as green. `gh pr checks` shows the STALE run from the previous
#      head and also looks green. land.sh now requires a non-zero run count
#      and refuses on DIRTY. Count the checks; absence is not success.
